# Site navigation checklist

When you add or rename a **public route**:

1. Register links in `composables/useSiteNav.ts` (`learnLinks`, `useLinks`, `metaLinks`, or `newHereCards` as appropriate).
2. Wire `AppHeader.vue` / `AppFooter.vue` only through `useSiteNav` (`headerLinks`, `footerSpecLinks`, `footerFollowLinks`, `toolsNav`) — do not duplicate URL arrays in components.
3. Add the route to [`config/staticRoutes.ts`](config/staticRoutes.ts) (prerender + sitemap import this list; `/rss.xml` stays dynamic).
4. Update the **Site map** table in root `README.md`.
5. **FAQ:** edit only the `faq` array in `useSiteNav.ts`. Update [`docs/SUPPORT.md`](docs/SUPPORT.md) only when routes, utilities, or Issues policy change — not FAQ body text.
6. For template-only downloads, update `templates/README.md` (synced to `public/templates/` on build).

Support channel: **GitHub Issues only** (templates under `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/`).
